FFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]monitor_continuations.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/monitor_continuations.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-zl[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-zl/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reproduce failures and measure continuation costs[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]baseline[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]baseline: add deterministic replay, evidence and lifecycle fixtures plus[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]component-level prompt measurements and shadow budget checks.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Define the Rust continuation and result contracts[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]after baseline[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: implement versioned exact-identity records, deterministic [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]replay planning, evidence policies and typed budget decisions with PyO3 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bindings.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Persist local deltas and handoff checkpoints[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capture[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture: capture provenance during expansion and persist immutable local[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]turns, exact parents and checkpoints across normal and interrupted [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]endings.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reconstruct ancestry without recursive transcript replay[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]replay[dim] · [dim][/dim]after capture[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]replay: integrate unique-node serial replay, exact fork targets, stable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]blocks and a conservative immutable-history compatibility reader.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Preserve structured verification evidence[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]diagnostics[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]diagnostics: capture first-party stage results before temporary output [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]disappears and record bounded durable diagnostics and precise [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]log-retention metadata.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Deliver each monitor result once[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]results[dim] · [dim][/dim]after replay, diagnostics[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]results: freeze terminal results and apply auto, tail, file and none [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]policies consistently across successor, family and direct-reference [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]projections.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make outcome delivery durable and deduplicated[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]dispatch[dim] · [dim][/dim]after results[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]dispatch: persist outcome policies and delivery identities, deduplicate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]successor adoption, and reconcile crashes while preserving claims and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cancellation.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prepare conditional completion declarations[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]prepare[dim] · [dim][/dim]after dispatch[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prepare: add a host-sealed completion intent with repository decisions, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]verification requirements, state fingerprints and prepared result text.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Complete eligible verification through the host[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]completion[dim] · [dim][/dim]after prepare[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]completion: consume valid success intents through existing finalizers [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]without a model turn and route stale or failed completion into durable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]recovery.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bound continuation context without losing instructions[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]budgets[dim] · [dim][/dim]after results[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]budgets: enforce expanded-prompt budgets, reuse explicit checkpoints at [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]thresholds, preserve essential context and expose actionable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]nonlaunchable outcomes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Present a coherent monitor workflow[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]experience[dim] · [dim][/dim]after completion, budgets[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]experience: expose the profile and evidence controls, implement compact [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]result and continuation views in CLI and ACE, and synchronize [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]documentation and skill sources.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Validate the combined feature and activate it[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]release[dim] · [dim][/dim]after experience[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]release: exercise failure recovery and visual contracts, evaluate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]task-level efficiency, activate the complete feature with a defined [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]compatibility route and verify coordinated Rust and Python delivery.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-zl","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-zl.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-aeba9f28ad5f91eaf56231d8d1fa2ffb","started_at":"2026-09-11T10:32:31.940810+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"568bc21cba63421569875d85fc4fb8e4810159c1cc3c53ff6b28b0d98d2adf00","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-zl.11/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"afd489131d1dff40d698230f779cf6d60b825ab8e6336bd3a367c59bd4dd524b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-zl.11/meta.json","size_bytes":637},"prompt":{"digest":"01d133a5fde49dc55583113c7bab626397b2374ac7ba65d7d6b2f134ba00f72b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-zl.11/prompt.md","size_bytes":175},"state":{"digest":"f8b025fa36ddd90c14495631982f84e9ae4a5fde0820105f705c8a204a0fa934","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-zl.11/state.json","size_bytes":163}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-zl.11","local_name":"sase-zl.11","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-zl","agent_clan_generation":"20260911063143","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-zl.11","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-zl","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-zl.11","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-bf1c87fdf8bdd7840e1853ae20eabc94","started_at":"20260911063153","state":"waiting"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true